<UserControl
    x:Class="StremioVideoCenter.StremioVideoCenterSettingsView"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <Grid>

        <!-- ========================================================= -->
        <!-- MAIN SETTINGS PANEL (SCROLLABLE)                          -->
        <!-- ========================================================= -->
        <!--
            Added to fix content that grows taller than the settings window
            once test buttons produce multi-line results (Source
            Normalisation in particular could scroll fully off-screen with
            no way to reach it). Vertical-only: horizontal scrolling is
            explicitly disabled since nothing in this layout needs it.
            Mouse wheel scrolling works automatically with ScrollViewer -
            no extra wiring required. No Background/Foreground set here, so
            the existing dark appearance (inherited from Playnite's theme
            resources) is completely unaffected.
        -->
        <ScrollViewer
            VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
            HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">

        <StackPanel Margin="10">

            <!-- ========================================================= -->
            <!-- TITLE                                                     -->
            <!-- ========================================================= -->

            <TextBlock
                Text="Stremio Video Center"
                FontWeight="Bold"
                FontSize="16"
                Margin="0,0,0,20"/>


            <!-- ========================================================= -->
            <!-- REAL-DEBRID SETTINGS                                       -->
            <!-- ========================================================= -->
            <!--
                OMDb's settings section was removed in the Cinemeta-First
                Addon Settings Architecture slice - it was confirmed dead
                beyond this panel's own test button (never read by
                CatalogueService/HeroRecommendationService/Home). OmdbApiKey
                and OmdbService.cs themselves are left completely intact in
                the backend per project rule (do not delete working code
                that isn't proven safe to remove) - only the user-facing
                controls are gone.

                This Real-Debrid section is KEPT, not removed, even though
                Torrentio/Comet manifest URLs can carry their own baked-in
                RD keys. Re-audited in a later correction pass, specifically
                to check whether this standalone section was still
                necessary now that Torrentio/Comet are configured via their
                own manifest URLs. Findings (see
                claude/Cinemeta_First_Addon_Settings_Architecture.md for the
                full write-up):

                1. RealDebridApiKey is the ONLY source of an RD credential
                   anywhere in Zino's own code - nothing parses or reuses
                   whatever RD key a user baked into a Torrentio/Comet
                   manifest URL when configuring those addons on their own
                   pages (and the addon protocol gives Zino no way to read
                   that key even if it wanted to - it only ever sees each
                   addon's resulting stream).
                2. StreamResolverService.ResolveStreamAsync shows exactly
                   when each credential matters: a stream that already
                   arrives with a direct stream.Url (the addon resolved it
                   server-side, using whatever RD key was in ITS manifest)
                   plays with no Zino RD token involved at all. A stream
                   that instead arrives as stream.InfoHash (a raw
                   torrent/magnet Torrentio or Comet did not itself
                   resolve) is handed to Zino's OWN RealDebridService,
                   built from this RealDebridApiKey - and that call throws
                   immediately if this field is empty.
                3. This applies identically to Torrentio and Comet - both
                   go through the exact same generic pipeline, with no
                   provider-specific branching anywhere in
                   StreamResolverService/RealDebridService.

                So the addon's own manifest-level RD configuration cannot
                substitute for this field: whether it's needed depends on
                the individual stream, not on which addon returned it or
                how that addon itself is configured. Removing this section
                would break playback of every InfoHash-based stream from
                either addon.
            -->

            <TextBlock
                Text="Real-Debrid"
                FontWeight="Bold"
                FontSize="14"
                Margin="0,0,0,8"/>

            <TextBlock
                Text="Real-Debrid API Token"
                Margin="0,0,0,5"/>

            <PasswordBox
                x:Name="RealDebridApiKeyBox"
                Height="28"
                Margin="0,0,0,5"
                PasswordChanged="RealDebridApiKeyBox_PasswordChanged"/>

            <StackPanel>

                <TextBlock
                    Text="Used to resolve torrent/magnet-based Stremio streams into direct playable links. This is a separate credential from any Real-Debrid key you configured inside Torrentio or Comet's own manifest URL - it is still required here for any stream those addons return unresolved (as a torrent/magnet rather than a ready direct link)."
                    Opacity="0.65"
                    FontSize="11"
                    TextWrapping="Wrap"
                    Margin="0,0,0,8"/>

                <Button
                    x:Name="TestRealDebridConnectionButton"
                    Content="Test Real-Debrid Connection"
                    Width="180"
                    Height="30"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                    Click="TestRealDebridConnection_Click"/>

                <TextBlock
                    x:Name="RealDebridConnectionStatus"
                    Margin="0,8,0,0"
                    FontSize="11"
                    TextWrapping="Wrap"/>

            </StackPanel>


            <!--
                "Test Content Discovery" (a diagnostic button that proved
                the catalogue -> Stremio content-id pipeline for a movie/TV
                episode/anime episode against the local test addon) was
                removed here in Slice 13 (Cinemeta-First Provider & Addon
                Architecture) - inspection confirmed it was purely a
                diagnostic control (never part of the real playback path;
                PlaySelectedMediaAsync in StremioVideoCenterView.xaml.cs
                builds its own ContentRequest directly from the selected
                MediaItem, it never went through this test's lookup
                code). Real content discovery is now exercised by the
                actual Cinemeta-first catalogue/episode-browsing/playback
                pipeline this slice implements, not a separate button.

                The legacy "Stremio Addons" free-text section (a multiline
                textbox of manifest URLs, defaulting to the local test
                addon at 127.0.0.1:7000, plus a "Test Configured Addons"
                button) was removed from this user-facing panel in an
                earlier correction pass - the "Other Addons" installer
                below is now the one user-facing way to add a manifest
                URL, and having both was a duplicate configuration
                mechanism.

                Nothing about the underlying Settings.StremioAddonUrls
                field or its default value was touched: it is still read
                automatically (StremioVideoCenterSettings.SyncLegacyAddonUrls
                migrates it into AddonInstances on load/save, and
                StremioVideoCenterView.xaml.cs still falls back to it
                directly at playback time). Only the dedicated free-text
                editing UI, its own "test" button, and (this slice) the
                Content Discovery diagnostic above are gone.
            -->

            <!-- ========================================================= -->
            <!-- ADDON MANAGEMENT                                           -->
            <!-- ========================================================= -->
            <!--
                Structured addon instances (Models.AddonInstance), additive
                to the legacy "Stremio Addons" section above - that section
                and its StremioAddonUrls setting are left completely
                untouched. Torrentio and Comet are "Recommended" here only
                in the sense that Zino gives them a one-click path to their
                own configuration page; every instance below (Recommended
                or Custom) is installed through the exact same generic
                "fetch + validate manifest.json" flow - there is no
                addon-specific logic anywhere in this section.
            -->

            <TextBlock
                Text="Addon Management"
                FontWeight="Bold"
                FontSize="14"
                Margin="0,20,0,8"/>

            <TextBlock
                Text="Cinemeta, AnimeFLV, OpenSubtitles, OpenSubtitles v3 and Local Files are installed automatically as Zino's core addons - see the Installed Addon Instances list below. Torrentio and Comet are recommended stream providers configured entirely on their own page - Zino never reproduces that page. Open it, configure your preferences there, then paste the manifest URL it gives you back here. Re-pasting a new URL replaces the previous configuration; it never creates a duplicate entry."
                Opacity="0.65"
                FontSize="11"
                TextWrapping="Wrap"
                Margin="0,0,0,14"/>

            <!--
                Torrentio/Comet button states (correction pass): the top
                button reads "Configure & Install..." when nothing is
                configured yet, or "Reconfigure" once an instance exists -
                both open the provider's own configuration page, since
                reconfiguring means going back there for a fresh manifest
                URL. A "Remove" button appears alongside it only once
                configured. Both are toggled from code-behind
                (RefreshAddonInstancesList/ApplyProviderButtonState) since
                this project does not use XAML triggers/converters for
                this kind of state. Widths are shared between Torrentio
                and Comet and sized so neither label is ever clipped.
            -->

            <!-- Torrentio -->
            <TextBlock
                Text="Torrentio"
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Margin="0,0,0,4"/>

            <TextBlock
                x:Name="TorrentioCurrentStatus"
                Text="Not configured."
                Opacity="0.6"
                FontSize="11"
                Margin="0,0,0,6"/>

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,6">
                <Button
                    x:Name="TorrentioConfigureButton"
                    Content="Configure &amp; Install..."
                    Width="190"
                    Height="28"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                    Click="TorrentioConfigure_Click"/>
                <Button
                    x:Name="TorrentioRemoveButton"
                    Content="Remove"
                    Width="90"
                    Height="28"
                    Margin="6,0,0,0"
                    Visibility="Collapsed"
                    Click="TorrentioRemove_Click"/>
            </StackPanel>

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,4">
                <TextBox
                    x:Name="TorrentioManifestUrlBox"
                    Width="380"
                    Height="26"/>
                <Button
                    x:Name="TorrentioInstallButton"
                    Content="Install"
                    Width="90"
                    Height="26"
                    Margin="6,0,0,0"
                    Click="TorrentioInstall_Click"/>
            </StackPanel>

            <TextBlock
                x:Name="TorrentioInstallStatus"
                Margin="0,4,0,16"
                FontSize="11"
                TextWrapping="Wrap"/>

            <!-- Comet -->
            <TextBlock
                Text="Comet"
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Margin="0,0,0,4"/>

            <TextBlock
                x:Name="CometCurrentStatus"
                Text="Not configured."
                Opacity="0.6"
                FontSize="11"
                Margin="0,0,0,6"/>

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,6">
                <Button
                    x:Name="CometConfigureButton"
                    Content="Configure &amp; Install..."
                    Width="190"
                    Height="28"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                    Click="CometConfigure_Click"/>
                <Button
                    x:Name="CometRemoveButton"
                    Content="Remove"
                    Width="90"
                    Height="28"
                    Margin="6,0,0,0"
                    Visibility="Collapsed"
                    Click="CometRemove_Click"/>
            </StackPanel>

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,4">
                <TextBox
                    x:Name="CometManifestUrlBox"
                    Width="380"
                    Height="26"/>
                <Button
                    x:Name="CometInstallButton"
                    Content="Install"
                    Width="90"
                    Height="26"
                    Margin="6,0,0,0"
                    Click="CometInstall_Click"/>
            </StackPanel>

            <TextBlock
                x:Name="CometInstallStatus"
                Margin="0,4,0,16"
                FontSize="11"
                TextWrapping="Wrap"/>

            <!-- Custom -->
            <TextBlock
                Text="Other Addons"
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Margin="0,0,0,4"/>

            <TextBlock
                Text="Add any other Stremio-compatible addon by its manifest URL (base URL or the full .../manifest.json). Multiple instances are allowed here, unlike Torrentio/Comet above."
                Opacity="0.65"
                FontSize="11"
                TextWrapping="Wrap"
                Margin="0,0,0,4"/>

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,4">
                <TextBox
                    x:Name="CustomManifestUrlBox"
                    Width="380"
                    Height="26"/>
                <Button
                    x:Name="CustomInstallButton"
                    Content="Add Addon"
                    Width="90"
                    Height="26"
                    Margin="6,0,0,0"
                    Click="CustomInstall_Click"/>
            </StackPanel>

            <TextBlock
                x:Name="CustomInstallStatus"
                Margin="0,4,0,16"
                FontSize="11"
                TextWrapping="Wrap"/>

            <!-- Installed instances -->
            <TextBlock
                Text="Installed Addon Instances"
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Margin="0,4,0,4"/>

            <TextBlock
                x:Name="NoAddonInstancesText"
                Text="No addons installed yet."
                Opacity="0.5"
                FontSize="11"
                Margin="0,0,0,8"/>

            <ItemsControl
                x:Name="AddonInstancesItemsControl"
                Margin="0,0,0,8">
                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate>
                        <Border
                            BorderBrush="#33FFFFFF"
                            BorderThickness="0,0,0,1"
                            Padding="0,6,0,6"
                            Margin="0,0,0,2">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                                <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <TextBlock
                                        Text="{Binding FriendlyName}"
                                        FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                        FontSize="12"/>
                                    <!--
                                        Category only - NEVER ManifestUrl. For
                                        a Real-Debrid-configured addon
                                        (Torrentio, Comet, or any manifest URL
                                        with baked-in credentials) that URL is
                                        a secret and must never be displayed
                                        here (Cinemeta-First Addon Settings
                                        Architecture slice, Part 9).
                                    -->
                                    <TextBlock
                                        Text="{Binding Category}"
                                        FontSize="10"
                                        Opacity="0.6"
                                        TextWrapping="Wrap"/>
                                </StackPanel>

                                <CheckBox
                                    Grid.Column="1"
                                    Content="Enabled"
                                    IsChecked="{Binding Enabled, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                    VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                    Margin="8,0,8,0"/>

                                <Button
                                    Grid.Column="2"
                                    Content="Remove"
                                    Width="70"
                                    Height="24"
                                    VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                    Tag="{Binding}"
                                    Click="RemoveAddonInstance_Click"/>
                            </Grid>
                        </Border>
                    </DataTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            </ItemsControl>

            <!--
                The internal diagnostic sections that used to appear here
                (Source Aggregation, Source Normalisation, and the
                dependency-free Self-Checks) were removed from this
                user-facing Settings page in this correction pass - they
                were development-only tools, not something Zino's actual
                users need. Their code-behind handlers
                (TestSourceAggregation_Click, FormatAggregationResult,
                TestSourceNormalisation_Click, RedactUrlIfNeeded,
                FormatFileSize, RunSelfChecks_Click) were unused anywhere
                else and were removed with them.
                PlaybackSourceAggregationService and
                PlaybackSourceNormalizationService themselves - the actual
                production services those buttons exercised - are
                untouched; they remain in active use by the real
                playback/browsing pipeline
                (StremioVideoCenterView.xaml.cs, EpisodeBrowserView.xaml.cs,
                CatalogueService.cs).
            -->

        </StackPanel>

        </ScrollViewer>

    </Grid>

</UserControl>